# UI stack policy

- Do not create new UIs with Unity UI Toolkit (`UIDocument`, UXML, USS, UI Toolkit controllers).
- Treat existing UI Toolkit screens as legacy/transitional; avoid expanding them unless explicitly requested.
- Prefer uGUI (`Canvas`, `RectTransform`, `Image`, `Button`, `TMP_Text`) for all new gameplay and menu UI work.
- For temporary test interfaces, build runtime debug UI with uGUI and keep it isolated so it can be removed later.

# When migrating/replacing old UI Toolkit screens

- Keep logic separated from view so the final uGUI screen can replace the temporary screen without gameplay changes.
- Reuse existing controllers/services when possible; only swap view layer and bindings.

# Exceptions

- Use UI Toolkit only if the user explicitly asks for it in that task.
